## Two different login systems

Staff and parents use different login methods, even though they're on related apps:

- **Staff** (the school dashboard) log in with a username and password, and their session is kept
  alive automatically in the background for as long as they keep using the dashboard.
- **Parents** (the parent portal) verify with a one-time code (OTP) sent to their phone/email the
  first time, then log in with a password afterwards — see
  [Getting Started as a Parent](/docs/shared-parent-getting-started).
- **Admissions applicants** also use an OTP-based login, separate from both of the above, scoped
  to that institute's admissions process.

## Why you might get logged out

Session length differs by institute type, and refreshing your session happens automatically in
the background — you shouldn't normally need to log in again mid-session. If you *are* logged out
unexpectedly:

- On the staff dashboard, this is usually a genuinely expired session — log back in normally.
- On the parent portal, an expired session can sometimes show as a generic error rather than a
  clear "please log in again" message. If something looks broken rather than showing a login
  prompt, try logging in again directly before assuming a feature is broken.

